    <h3 id="solution">Solution</h3>

<p>To solve the puzzle, you must iterate over the specified private keyspace and check the balance of each private key.
    The narrower the keyspace, the greater the chance of finding the private key. Currently, it is better
    to focus on solving puzzle #71 (due to its narrower keyspace) or #140
    (utilizing the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby-step_giant-step">Baby-step giant-step</a> or <a
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pollard%27s_kangaroo_algorithm">Pollard's kangaroo</a>
    algorithm because of the exposed public key).</p>

<p>To automate this process, you can use the following methods and tools:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Use our <a href="/bitcoin-puzzle-solver"><strong>Bitcoin Puzzle Solver</strong></a></li>
    <li>Browse <a href="/keys/bitcoin/puzzle-71">private keys
            directory</a> of the puzzle #71 (not highly effective)
    </li>
    <li>Generate <a href="/keys/bitcoin/puzzle-71/random">
            random keys</a> within the keyspace of puzzle #71 (not highly effective)
    </li>
    <li>Use <a href="https://github.com/albertobsd/keyhunt">KeyHunt</a> for CPU search
        (<a data-bs-toggle="collapse" href="#keyhunt" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="keyhunt">example</a>)
        <div class="collapse mt-3" id="keyhunt">
            <p>71-bit puzzle search:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>./keyhunt -m rmd160 -f 71.rmd -b 71 -l compress -R</code></pre>

            <p>Contents of the input file 71.rmd:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>f6f5431d25bbf7b12e8add9af5e3475c44a0a5b8</code></pre>

            <p>140-bit puzzle (BSGS) search:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>./keyhunt -m bsgs -f 140.txt -b 140 -R</code></pre>

            <p>Contents of the input file 140.txt:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>031f6a332d3c5c4f2de2378c012f429cd109ba07d69690c6c701b6bb87860d6640</code></pre>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        Use <a href="https://github.com/RetiredC/RCKangaroo">RCKangaroo</a> for GPU search
        (<a data-bs-toggle="collapse" href="#rckangaroo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="rckangaroo">example</a>)
        <div class="collapse mt-3" id="rckangaroo">
            <p>140-bit puzzle search:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>RCKangaroo.exe -dp 16 -range 139 -start 80000000000000000000000000000000000 -pubkey 031f6a332d3c5c4f2de2378c012f429cd109ba07d69690c6c701b6bb87860d6640</code></pre>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <s>Use <a href="https://github.com/JeanLucPons/Kangaroo">Kangaroo</a> for GPU search puzzles with exposed
            public key (limited to a 125-bit interval search)</s>
        (<a data-bs-toggle="collapse" href="#kangaroo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="kangaroo">example</a>)
        <div class="collapse mt-3" id="kangaroo">
            <p>125-bit puzzle search:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>./Kangaroo -gpu 125.txt</code></pre>
            <p>Contents of the input file 125.txt:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>10000000000000000000000000000000
1fffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
0233709eb11e0d4439a729f21c2c443dedb727528229713f0065721ba8fa46f00e</code></pre>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        Use <a href="https://github.com/brichard19/BitCrack">BitCrack</a> for GPU search
        (<a data-bs-toggle="collapse" href="#bitcrack" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="bitcrack">example</a>)
        <div class="collapse mt-3" id="bitcrack">
            <p>71-bit puzzle search:</p>
            <pre class="code-block"><button class="copy" title="Copy" data-bs-toggle="tooltip"><i class="far fa-copy"></i></button><code>xxBitCrack.exe --keyspace 400000000000000000:7fffffffffffffffff -c 1PWo3JeB9jrGwfHDNpdGK54CRas7fsVzXU</code></pre>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>Join one of the collective solving pools</li>
</ul>

